    "background_story": "Martha was a free-spirited artist, often lost in her own world of creativity. Her oblivious nature made her both endearing and frustrating to those around her. She would forget appointments, misplace her keys, and sometimes even forget what day it was. Despite her absent-mindedness, Martha's art studio was a treasure trove of imagination and inspiration. Her friends and family had grown accustomed to her quirks, and they lovingly referred to her as 'spacey Martha.' One day, while working on a new project, Martha accidentally left her studio door open, and a stray cat wandered in. Unaware of the new visitor, Martha continued to paint, while the cat curled up beside her, purring contentedly. It wasn't until hours later that she noticed her new feline friend, and laughed at her own obliviousness.",
